  "id": "imitative-learning",
  "term": "imitative learning",
  "definition": "In this historical source, imitative learning means learning by copying the cues, signs, or expressions supplied by others rather than relying only on one’s own slow personal experience. In the child, it is described as being greatly aided by living in a society that already has spoken and written language.",
